{
  "about": "Store art v2 geometry (production spec sections 2.4, 3 and 7), canvas px on 1320x2868. card: the set's paper recipe, the game's Photo-mode polaroid (homeworld.ts renderPhoto): border = top and side paper, lip = the heavy bottom strip, radius = outer corner, winRadius = window corner; any card may override a field. Each card tilts about its window centre. cards: window x/y/w/h, raw crop origin sx/sy at scale (<= 1), tilt rot, tape [x, y, width, angle] (colour from the slot). stickers: name in the sticker dir, display width w incl. backing, centre x/y, tilt rot. '@arrival' = the species that arrived in m3-friend; '@shot1' = bunny if a bunny lives on planet P at NEW-1, else frog. Shot 8 card 2 is cropped to the modal's box from m8b-gate.json; gateRadius is the modal's own corner radius in raw px (border-radius 24 CSS px x DPR 3), and the window corners take gateRadius x crop scale so the backdrop never shows in the corners (a mask, not a repaint). Shot 7: fitRows ends the window in the gap under Lifebook row 5 (per locale, from capture-log m7.cards), and the trio is placed yFromBottom of that window, so it is stuck across the bottom lip and covers no creature or text. Shot 8 card 1 ends in the gap under the Play time section (raw y 730): the toggle rows below it render as shrink-wrapped pills in the shipped CSS, so they stay out of frame until that game fix lands.",
